    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d327">

                <pb facs="0290" n="284" xml:id="pg284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/4048: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-02-13T20:00:00-05:00">February 13, 1939—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>29. Your 95, February 11, 5 p.m., and Davies’ February 12, 1 p.m.<anchor n="94"
                        xml:id="d327-f1"/> Department desires that you make every practicable
                    endeavor to obtain the cooperation of the appropriate Chinese authorities in
                    arranging for the withdrawal of Americans from Kuling and that you make use of
                    such communication facilities as are available to urge Americans at Kuling to
                    withdraw if possible.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Davies, U.S.S. <hi rendition="#italic">Oahu</hi>, Shanghai, and
                    Hankow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
